<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd unit for HAFleet's own service supervisor, on macOS.

  WHY IT EXISTS. `bin/hafleet-acp-up` says the supervisor "is itself started by launchd or systemd". The
  systemd units in this repo start individual services rather than the supervisor, and on macOS there was
  no unit at all — so on this host nothing started it, and every service was launched by hand with
  `nohup`. Restart-on-crash and reboot survival were both built and unreachable.

  INSTALL (from the repo root, with the runtime .env sourced so the paths below are the ones you mean):

    mkdir -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents
    sed -e "s|__REPO__|$PWD|g" -e "s|__RUNTIME__|$HAFLEET_RUNTIME_DIR|g" \
        deploy/com.hafleet.supervisor.plist > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.hafleet.supervisor.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.hafleet.supervisor.plist

  STOP, and the difference matters: `launchctl bootout` removes the job, while `kill` on the process
  makes launchd start it again — which is the unit working, and reads as a supervisor that will not die.

  THE PLACEHOLDERS ARE NOT DEFAULTS. `__RUNTIME__` has no sensible fallback: a supervisor that guessed
  would serve a different fleet than the operator believes is running, and this session did exactly that
  by hand once — caught only by an agent count that looked wrong.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.hafleet.supervisor</string>

  <!--
    The entrypoint runs in the FOREGROUND and launchd owns it. A program that daemonises itself takes
    that ownership away, which is how you get a supervisor launchd cannot supervise.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/env</string>
    <string>node</string>
    <string>__REPO__/bin/hafleet-supervisor</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__REPO__</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HAFLEET_RUNTIME_DIR</key>
    <string>__RUNTIME__</string>
    <!--
      PATH is stated because launchd's is minimal and does NOT include the places node and the coding
      CLIs actually live. `hafleet-acp-up` records the same failure from the other side: without the
      framework binary's directory the host exits at once and the entry restarts forever.
    -->
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <!--
    KeepAlive on non-zero exit only. `SuccessfulExit: false` means launchd restarts a crash and leaves a
    clean stop alone — which is why the entrypoint exits non-zero when it fails to start and 0 when it
    was asked to stop. Restarting an intentional shutdown would make `launchctl bootout` unusable.
  -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <!--
    Ten seconds between restarts. launchd's own floor is 10s and it will throttle anyway; stating it
    keeps a crash-looping supervisor from filling the log faster than anyone can read it, and the
    supervisor has its own per-service backoff underneath this.
  -->
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>

  <!--
    Logs go to the RUNTIME directory, not the repo: they are runtime state, and a repo that collects
    logs is a repo whose diffs fill with them.
  -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__RUNTIME__/logs/supervisor.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__RUNTIME__/logs/supervisor.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
